{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556719117,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODI4OTMwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3370#issuecomment-488289307"},"message":"sounds reasonable!  Given that commit message is kinda static and we do not show up a dialog to have commit message tuned up before recording it, I wonder what value is in `Do not change lines below`? Even if we showed the commit message, we could use git way to annotate it with comments regarding the block which shouldn't be modified.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556719695,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODI5MTgwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3370#issuecomment-488291807"},"message":"As for tagging - started a dedicated https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3371 . As we agreed, shouldn't be a part of the commit record.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556722776,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODMwNjM0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3370#issuecomment-488306342"},"message":"I'm in favor of modifying the record markup lines to be more specific for run as well as detecting run commits with those markers alone.  For the specific markup, I'm OK with the one above (with a slight preference for s/CMD/RUN/), but it's worth thinking about more because we're committed to it even if we switch to something else.\n\nEven without requiring the subject prefix for detection, there's the question of whether we want to use it at all.  I agree with the suggestion here to drop it when there is a user-supplied message.  If there isn't, presumably we should use one of the suggestions from #3062?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556723276,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODMwODU0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3370#issuecomment-488308540"},"message":"@yarikoptic:\n\n\u003e Given that commit message is kinda static and we do not show up a dialog to have commit message tuned up before recording it, I wonder what value is in `Do not change lines below`?\n\nGiven that we need some sort of markup for detection and readability, I think we might as well use that markup to make it clear that those lines shouldn't be touched because there's is nothing wrong with a user doing something like 'git commit --only --amend' to adjust the message (with all the usual caveats about rewriting published history).","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556723276,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDIxNjg2MDQ5Mw=="},"target":"be0e871f30020073e934460375cd0c089ceb768ef493bbf2c40acaa6b734d7c6","message":"@yarikoptic:\n\n\u003e Given that commit message is kinda static and we do not show up a dialog to have commit message tuned up before recording it, I wonder what value is in `Do not change lines below`?\n\nGiven that we need some sort of markup for detection and readability, I think we might as well use that markup to make it clear that those lines shouldn't be touched because there's nothing wrong with a user doing something like 'git commit --only --amend' to adjust the message (with all the usual caveats about rewriting published history).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556725209,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODMxODY5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3370#issuecomment-488318693"},"message":"I said:\n\n\u003e [...] there's is nothing wrong with a user doing something like 'git commit --only --amend' to adjust the message (with all the usual caveats about rewriting published history).\n\nTo add to that: Even outside of run, I use the above to work around DataLad's lack of support for popping up a proper editor for writing the message.","files":null}]}